Package: BiocJobs
Title: Declare and Dispatch Batch Jobs from Bioconductor Packages
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bioconductor", "Core Team",
           email = "maintainer@bioconductor.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: A lightweight framework for Bioconductor package developers to
    declare non-interactive, dispatchable units of work ("jobs") inside their
    packages. A job is an R script plus a YAML specification of its inputs,
    outputs, configuration options, and resource requirements, shipped under
    inst/biocjobs/. BiocJobs discovers and validates these specifications, runs
    jobs locally, and automatically generates execution artifacts for
    workflow infrastructure: GA4GH Task Execution Service (TES) task
    definitions and Galaxy tool wrappers, with more targets to follow.
License: Artistic-2.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.4.0)
Imports:
    yaml,
    jsonlite,
    xml2,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    BiocManager
biocViews: Infrastructure, Software
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
